## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
| --- | --- |
| Web app | React 19, Vite 8, React Router 8, TanStack Query 5, react-i18next (ICU), TypeScript 6 |
| Design system | Tailwind CSS 4, Radix primitives, Storybook 10 with accessibility tests |
| API | Python 3.14, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.1 (async), Alembic, Pydantic 2 |
| Data | PostgreSQL 18 (RDS in AWS, Docker locally) |
| Auth | Amazon Cognito (hosted sign-in, authorization code + PKCE), JWT authorizer on API Gateway |
| AWS | API Gateway HTTP API, Lambda (arm64, SnapStart), RDS, S3 + CloudFront, deployed with SAM |
| Tooling | npm workspaces, uv, ESLint 10, Prettier, ruff, mypy, Vitest 5, pytest, GitHub Actions |

## Quick start

You need Node 24, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), and Docker.

```bash
npm ci
(cd apps/backend && uv sync && cp .env.example .env)
docker compose up -d db
(cd apps/backend && uv run alembic upgrade head)
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173. Locally everyone is signed in as a fixed developer user,
so no AWS account is needed. The full walkthrough is in
[docs/dev_guides/onboarding/1_FIRST_TIME_SETUP.md](docs/dev_guides/onboarding/1_FIRST_TIME_SETUP.md).

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | API on :8000 and web app on :5173 with hot reload |
| `npm run storybook` | UI kit component explorer on :6006 |
| `npm run lint` / `npm run format` | ESLint and Prettier for all TypeScript |
| `npm run typecheck` | TypeScript in every workspace |
| `npm test` | Unit tests in every workspace, with coverage floors |
| `npm run test:stories -w @app/ui-kit` | Every story in Chromium with axe accessibility checks |
| `npm run gen:api` | Regenerate `apps/backend/openapi.json` and the frontend API types |
| `cd apps/backend && uv run pytest` | Backend unit and integration tests |
| `cd apps/backend && uv run ruff check . && uv run mypy && uv run lint-imports` | Backend lint, types, and import rules |

## Layout

```
apps/
  backend/        FastAPI app, migrations, tests, SAM templates (template.yaml, infra/)
  frontend/       React app and its hosting template (template.yaml)
packages/
  ui-kit/         Design system: tokens, components, Storybook
  shared/         Non-UI TypeScript shared by apps: API errors, query client, test helpers
infra/            One-time AWS account bootstrap (GitHub deploy role)
docs/             Architecture, decisions, security, guides, runbooks
.implementation_plans/  Phased plans for features in progress
.github/          CI, deploy, CodeQL, dependency audit, Dependabot
```

